From 24198297c1955f8acc0839db85c250ddc5dc6e77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alfonso Fortunato <57877156+devopsfortunato@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:15:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Enable fused draft metadata updates for the QSA side
 cache

Upstream PR vllm-project/vllm#58449 (head 848dbf89ec), applied with
git apply --3way on top of 781c2cbcb7.

QSAMetadataBuilder gains supports_draft_decode_metadata_update = HAS_TRITON
and update_draft_decode_metadata(), which re-launches the existing Triton
side-cache build kernel in place (capture-safe: fixed shapes/scalars, no
CPU reads inside the launch path). The speculator (vllm/v1/worker/gpu/
spec_decode/speculator.py:328) previously saw the QSA group unsupported
and rebuilt QSA attention metadata eagerly on every MTP draft step
('QWEN4_EXP_EXP_QSA_STATE cannot update draft decode metadata in place;
falling back to rebuilding attention metadata eagerly').

Fork comparison: the fork avoids the eager rebuild through its merged
B12x QSA owner (src-cmp/fork vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/b12x_qsa.py:214,297)
where the selector state is updated transactionally inside the fused
qwen4_exp_b12x_qsa_with_output custom op; its update_draft_decode_metadata
only resets qsa_num_accepted_tokens. This patch gives the v0.32 Triton
side-cache path the same no-eager-rebuild property. Extra piece the fork
has that #58449 lacks: the fork's AttentionCGSupport.ALWAYS builder and
B12xPagedMetadata builder chain also capture the per-request QSA state
(slot ids, is_fresh, accepted tokens) into persistent device buffers, so
nothing at all is rebuilt between draft steps; #58449 still re-launches
the Triton build kernel per draft step (in-graph, not rebuilt via CPU).
